---
import GuideDemo from './GuideDemo.astro'

const sources = [
  { key: 'crawl', name: 'Crawl' },
  { key: 'gsc', name: 'Search Console' },
  { key: 'analytics', name: 'Analytics' },
  { key: 'live', name: 'Live results' },
]

const findings = [
  {
    key: 'crawl',
    source: 'Crawl',
    text: 'The pricing page loads, returns 200, and nothing on it blocks search engines. The problem is not technical.',
  },
  {
    key: 'gsc',
    source: 'Search Console',
    text: 'Clicks fell from 480 to 210 in four weeks while impressions held. The page lost position, not demand.',
  },
  {
    key: 'analytics',
    source: 'Analytics',
    text: 'The visitors who still arrive behave the same as before. The drop is in arrivals, not on the page.',
  },
  {
    key: 'live',
    source: 'Live results',
    text: 'A competitor comparison page now sits above yours for the main query. That is where the clicks went.',
  },
]

const toggleClasses =
  'group flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 border-2 border-nav bg-background px-3 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs transition-colors hover:bg-background-subtle focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary'
---

<GuideDemo
  number="01"
  label="The evidence"
  title="Every claim names its source"
  description="One question, four sources. Disconnect a source and watch which parts of the answer the agent can no longer make."
>
  <div x-data="evidenceSources" class="space-y-5">
    <p class="font-sans text-sm leading-6">
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-mono text-primary">&rsaquo;</span>
      Why did clicks fall on the pricing page this month?
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2" role="group" aria-label="Evidence sources">
      {
        sources.map((source) => (
          <button
            type="button"
            class={toggleClasses}
            aria-pressed="true"
            x-on:click={`toggle('${source.key}')`}
            x-bind:aria-pressed={`sources.${source.key} ? 'true' : 'false'`}
          >
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="size-2 border border-current bg-primary group-aria-[pressed=false]:bg-transparent"
            />
            {source.name}
          </button>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <ul class="space-y-2">
      {
        findings.map((finding) => (
          <li
            class="border-2 border-border bg-background p-3"
            x-bind:hidden={`!sources.${finding.key}`}
          >
            <p class="mb-1 font-mono text-[0.625rem] uppercase tracking-wide text-foreground-faint">
              Observed &middot; {finding.source}
            </p>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm font-light leading-6">{finding.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
      <li
        hidden
        class="border-2 border-dashed border-border p-3 font-sans text-sm font-light leading-6 text-foreground-muted"
        x-bind:hidden="!allOff()"
      >
        With nothing connected, the agent can still write plausible advice. So can any chatbot. The evidence is the difference.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p aria-live="polite" class="font-mono text-xs text-foreground-muted">
      <span x-text="caption()">All four sources connected. Every claim below names the evidence behind it.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</GuideDemo>

<div hidden data-agent-markdown="only">
  <p>
    Interactive demo: one question, "Why did clicks fall on the pricing page this month?", answered from four
    separate evidence sources. The crawl shows the page is technically fine. Search Console shows clicks fell
    while impressions held, so the page lost position, not demand. Analytics shows visitor behavior is unchanged,
    so the drop is in arrivals. Live results show a competitor page now ranks above it. Disconnecting a source
    removes the claims that depend on it, because one source cannot prove another's facts.
  </p>
</div>

<script>
  import './seo-agent.client'
</script>
